  "question": {
    "text": "A thin semi-circular ring of radius $r$ has a positive charge $q$ distributed uniformly over it. The net field $\\vec{E}$ at the centre $O$ is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6veO4pRmU1iB6s2CMj7T3Ufs9Zx3Zpp5ws8jDDQXIXU.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jwnLs",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{q}{4 \\pi^2 \\varepsilon_0 r^2} \\hat{j}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Uav2G",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{q}{4 \\pi^2 \\varepsilon_0 r^2} \\hat{j}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OWnYa",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{q}{2 \\pi^2 \\varepsilon_0 r^2} \\hat{j}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "goeJ3",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{2 \\pi^2 \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{r}^2} \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Linear charge density $\\lambda=\\left(\\frac{q}{\\pi r}\\right)$\n$E=\\int d E \\sin \\theta(-\\hat{\\mathrm{j}})=\\int \\frac{\\mathrm{K} \\cdot d q}{\\mathrm{r}^2} \\sin \\theta(-\\hat{\\mathrm{j}})$\n$\\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\mathrm{K}}{\\mathrm{r}^2} \\int \\frac{\\mathrm{qr}}{\\pi r} \\mathrm{~d} \\theta \\sin \\theta(-\\hat{\\mathrm{j}})$\n$=\\frac{\\mathrm{K}}{\\mathrm{r}^2} \\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{\\pi} \\int_0^\\pi \\sin \\theta(-\\hat{\\mathrm{j}})$\n$=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{2 \\pi^2 \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{r}^2}(-\\hat{\\mathrm{j}})$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/hVMGjVjZaHfEiDSqoB70ytJcuQ2SZ7rz0JvYo7K3Ehk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
